tool stdout: commit 22ebf75f3ce154279f7b4e0b8663c811159e4bd9
Author: Stefan Lindblad <stefan.lindblad@linux.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 6 01:09:04 2026 +0000

    agent-runner: top-edge-only panels, adaptive scrollbar, and theme support
    
    The transcript and prompt areas keep only their top edge (no left, right,
    or bottom borders), so each area gains one row and one column of content.
    All output uses the standard panel background (black in the default dark
    theme); thinking content is set apart by a left edge (block/bar) plus a
    muted tint, and highlighted code keeps its indentation plus a code patch,
    so both stand out without heavy boxing. A scrollbar is always present on
    the transcript's right edge, sized to the panel and tracking the current
    window into the full transcript (content length, viewport, offset).
    
    Theming now lives in tui::theme: one style table per built-in theme
    (dark default, light alternative) supplies every surface the shell draws,
    including the Markdown style table and code patch. The configuration
    theme key selects a theme (unknown names fail at load), --theme overrides
    it per run, and Ctrl+S cycles themes live, restyling existing transcript
    rows in place. Documented in the README, DESIGN.md, config example, and
    the help overlay.

