assistant: Now I have the full picture of the render side. Let me look at the transport internals (`get_bounded`, `connect`, deadline) to understand the discovery timeout.


provider reasoning: I found the key issue with ratatui's border rendering: when a block only has the TOP border set (without LEFT and RIGHT), the top border spans the full width with no corner characters. The problem is that the title gets rendered on top of the border line, which means it obscures the border characters beneath it.

So the top border line starts with the title text " transcript [n] " inlined, which pushes the horizontal dashes to begin a few cells in from the left edge. The user's request is asking for the top border to start with at least 1-2 horizontal line characters before the title, making it visually clear that the line is a border and not just text.

Looking at ratatui's implementation, it renders the title first, then fills the remaining space with border characters. To get those leading dashes before the title, I'd need to manually draw the top border row myself and place the title after a few leading dashes instead of relying on ratatui's `.title()` method.

For the second issue, the "model transport timed out" error happens because discovery only has a 5-second deadline, which is too short when llama-server is busy loading or switching models. The fix would be to give discovery the full per-turn deadline from the transport configuration, since it's the same kind of operation that might trigger a model load. I need to check the transport's deadline configuration and how `get_bounded` works to implement this properly.

