## What I found and fixed

**1. Model switch capacity-discovery timeout** (`agent_runtime/src/direct_transport.rs`)

The reported error comes from the serving-capacity probe (`DirectModelTransport::context_limit`), which is used to auto-detect a model's context window when neither `models.context_limit` nor `--context-limit` is set. It ran with a **hard 5-second** deadline (`self.deadline.min(Duration::from_secs(5))`). During a model *switch*, llama-server has to load/prefill the selected model before it answers even a bare metadata probe — for `qwen38-27b-q4-swift` that takes longer than 5s, so discovery timed out exactly as reported.

- Discovery now uses `self.deadline.min(MAX_CAPACITY_DISCOVERY)` with a new 60-second named bound, so a slow model load is waited out instead of failing. It's still far below a full turn deadline, and the 1 MiB response bound / loopback-only transport are unchanged.
- Updated the method doc, plus `agent_runtime/DESIGN.md` and `IMPL.md` which stated the "5-second" bound.

**2. Top borders starting with a horizontal-line lead** (`agent_runner/src/tui/render.rs`)

All five top-only panels (transcript, help, menu, sessions, replay) drew a `Borders::TOP` edge, but ratatui paints the left-aligned title *over* the first cells of the border, so the edge began with the title text instead of any `─`. I added a `panel_top_edge` helper that overlays the full edge after the panel renders: a **two-cell `──` lead**, then the title (kept in its native per-panel style — muted for the transcript, bold/cyan for the overlays), then the rest of the edge. Verified by rendering:
