    docs(agent_runner): specify active-model-first model selection
    
    Define model selection and activation as preferring the provider's
    already-loaded model over the static default, so an active model starts
    with no load/switch cost. The new behavior (requirements + contract +
    design-intent) is a bounded, read-only, loopback-only provider probe with
    this precedence:
    
      1. explicit selection (--model / in-TUI Tab) wins, never overridden
      2. a loaded provider model matching a configured entry is selected and
         announced (matched by provider model name, not the user-facing id);
         multiple loaded matches are ambiguous and fall to rule 4
      3. exactly one configured model auto-selects (single-choice convenience)
      4. several configured models with no active match: the TUI starts with no
         model selected (deferred load, existing prompt-hold machinery) and
         headless fails fast with an actionable diagnostic
    
    default_model stays a required field but becomes a last-resort fallback that
    never overrides an active model, an explicit selection, or a single model.
    An active provider model not present in [[models]] is offered as a
    ready-to-paste entry (as with --import-kvist) and never written to the config
    file automatically.
    
    Intent-only change: updates REQUIREMENTS.md (new RUN-REQ-MODEL-SELECTION
