provider reasoning: I'm seeing the TUI bootstrap flow now — when `tui::run` executes, it picks a model ID from the overrides or falls back to the default, spawns a background bootstrap with that model, and creates the App with that model's label. The key insight is that `App.model` gets set at construction, and when the user tabs to a new model, `cycle_model` updates `App.model` and the UI loop restarts the worker. So the "defer/no model" state would need `App.model` to be empty or None initially, with the bootstrap delayed until the user actually selects a model. That's a substantial refactor since the current design assumes a selected model is always present.

Looking at the project's TODO structure, the model-selection implementation is marked pending and has a write-tests dependency. The user is asking me to continue with this work. The core challenge is that the current App model has a non-Optional `model: String`, so "no model selected" isn't naturally representable without either changing that to an Option (a big change) or picking some initial model while not starting the bootstrap until the user tabs. I need to examine how the App model and bootstrap wiring actually work to figure out the minimal way to support deferral, then look at the existing model-selection tests to see if there are already some written.

